  "reason": "The pages kept noon reference instants computed with the browser’s time zone history and each zone’s reference-city mean time. The birth chart calculator reads the birthplace’s own local mean time and the pinned tzdb 2025c history with backzone before 1970, so 218 of the 501 pages gave a different instant from the calculator for the same place and date: 145 by ten minutes or less, 70 by between ten minutes and an hour, and 3 by a full hour. The methodology page named them as an exception.",
  "method": [
    "npx vite-node docs/phase5/people-pilot/tools/compute-astro.mjs --slug=<the 218>: the noon instant and both civil-day midnights now come from src/lib/time/localToUtc.ts with the birthplace’s longitude, as in ChartCalculator.",
    "Number-only edits to the 4 copy files that do not recompose identically from unchanged charts and state a changed number.",
    "node docs/phase5/people-pilot/tools/compose-copy.mjs --slug=<the other 98 pages whose stated facts changed>.",
    "node docs/phase5/people-pilot/tools/migrate-reference-instants.mjs --slug=<the 218>: chart-derived manifest fields only; portraits, sources, identity and eligibility unchanged.",
    "node scripts/build-people-pilot.mjs, and npm run data:og -- --only-people, keeping the 14 cards whose text changed."
